      {
        "id": "vZQJ4a4yVqrs0TYo",
        "title": "Designing an Experiment or Program to Figure Our what the Demo Gripper Does",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Right now the demo gripper is 0% closed. We want to figure out how it works: can we make it fully closed or partially closed?</p><p></p><p>Connect the gripper to your program (or to a different program you design!) and try to figure out:</p><ol><li><strong>How do you make the gripper close 100%?</strong></li><li><strong>Can you make the gripper partially closed? (e.g., 25% closed, 50% closed, 90% closed)</strong></li><li><strong>If no, why not? If yes, how? Is there a percent closed that it </strong><strong><em>can&#x27;t</em></strong><strong> do?</strong></li></ol><p></p><p>You might ask &quot;But what do I connect it to?&quot; or &quot;What is my program supposed to look like?&quot;</p><p>As you saw earlier, there isn&#x27;t just one way to make things work in programming!</p><p>Throughout these lessons, you will be developing strategies for designing and making new programs!</p><p></p><p><span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"52b0a17f-fac6-44ad-bf56-27b55ce9a7b7\"></span>: what numbers should you try to figure out the questions? What else should you do?</p><p><span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"64597ffb-c9a3-42be-9e5b-a1db70e7a26c\"></span>: what is a way to connect this to figure out the problem? Is there a simpler program you can make that will make it easier for you to figure out how to control the gripper?</p><p>If you&#x27;re not sure, try one way you can think of to connect it, even if you&#x27;re not sure it&#x27;s the best way. If it doesn&#x27;t help you, you can think about a better way later!</p>"
          ],
          "highlightedText": [
            {
              "id": "64597ffb-c9a3-42be-9e5b-a1db70e7a26c",
              "text": "Design your program"
            },
            {
              "id": "52b0a17f-fac6-44ad-bf56-27b55ce9a7b7",
              "text": "Design your Dataflow experiment"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
